user:
---
The target function is `rapidcsv::Document::InsertColumn`. Inserts a new column at `pColumnIdx` in the document. If `pColumn` is empty, it creates a blank column sized to current data rows; otherwise it converts values to strings and places them starting after the header row (`mLabelParams.mColumnNameIdx + 1`). `pColumnName` sets the column label. Its signature is as follows:

```cpp
/**
     * @brief   Insert column at specified index.
     * @param   pColumnIdx            zero-based column index.
     * @param   pColumn               vector of column data (optional argument).
     * @param   pColumnName           column label name (optional argument).
     */
template<typename T>
    void InsertColumn(const size_t pColumnIdx, const std::vector<T>& pColumn = std::vector<T>(),
                      const std::string& pColumnName = std::string());
```

The list of candidate functions from the library is:

1. `rapidcsv::Document::GetRow`
    `GetRow` returns a row as `std::vector<T>`, by row name or zero-based index, with optional conversion. If the named row isn’t found, it throws `std::out_of_range`. Example: `doc.GetRow<std::string>("2017-02-22")`. Its signature is:
    ```cpp
    /**
     * @brief   Get row by name.
     * @param   pRowName              row label name.
     * @param   pToVal                conversion function.
     * @returns vector of row data.
     */
template<typename T>
    std::vector<T> GetRow(const std::string& pRowName, ConvFunc<T> pToVal) const;
/**
     * @brief   Get row by index.
     * @param   pRowIdx               zero-based row index.
     * @returns vector of row data.
     */
template<typename T>
    std::vector<T> GetRow(const size_t pRowIdx) const;
/**
     * @brief   Get row by index.
     * @param   pRowIdx               zero-based row index.
     * @param   pToVal                conversion function.
     * @returns vector of row data.
     */
template<typename T>
    std::vector<T> GetRow(const size_t pRowIdx, ConvFunc<T> pToVal) const;
/**
     * @brief   Get row by name.
     * @param   pRowName              row label name.
     * @returns vector of row data.
     */
template<typename T>
    std::vector<T> GetRow(const std::string& pRowName) const;
    ```
2. `rapidcsv::Document::RemoveRow`
    Removes a row from the CSV document by zero-based data-row index or by row label. If the index maps past `mData.size()`, it throws `std::out_of_range`. After removal, row names are updated. Its signature is:
    ```cpp
    /**
     * @brief   Remove row by index.
     * @param   pRowIdx               zero-based row index.
     */
void RemoveRow(const size_t pRowIdx);
/**
     * @brief   Remove row by name.
     * @param   pRowName              row label name.
     */
void RemoveRow(const std::string& pRowName);
    ```
3. `rapidcsv::Converter::ToVal`
    `ToVal()` converts a CSV string to numeric `T` for `Converter`/`GetColumn<T>()` etc. Use by specializing/overriding it for custom types or behavior. It parses ints/longs/etc., checks range for small ints, and may throw on bad/out-of-range input. Example: `Converter<int>::ToVal()` in README; also refs `test035.cpp`. Its signature is:
    ```cpp
    /**
     * @brief   Converts string holding a numerical value to numerical datatype representation.
     * @param   pVal                  numerical value
     * @param   pStr                  output string
     */
void ToVal(const std::string& pStr, T& pVal) const;
    ```


