---
The target function is `rapidcsv::Document::GetRowCount`. `GetRowCount()` returns the number of data rows, excluding any label/header rows. Use it to query how many rows are available for row-based access. It computes `mData.size() - (mLabelParams.mColumnNameIdx + 1)` and returns `0` if that would be negative. Its signature is as follows:

```cpp
/**
     * @brief   Get number of data rows (excluding label rows).
     * @returns row count.
     */
size_t GetRowCount() const;
```

The list of candidate functions from the library is:

1. `rapidcsv::Document::GetColumnCount`
    Returns the number of data columns, excluding row-label columns. It uses the first data row (or `mColumnNameIdx` if set) and subtracts `mRowNameIdx+1`. If there’s no data or the result is negative, it returns 0. Its signature is:
    ```cpp
    /**
     * @brief   Get number of data columns (excluding label columns).
     * @returns column count.
     */
size_t GetColumnCount() const;
    ```
2. `rapidcsv::Document::GetColumnNames`
    `GetColumnNames()` returns the CSV’s column labels from the header row, or `{}` if no column-name row is configured/available. Use it to inspect/exist-check names (e.g. `find`). No special caveats noted. Its signature is:
    ```cpp
    /**
     * @brief   Get column names
     * @returns vector of column names.
     */
std::vector<std::string> GetColumnNames() const;
    ```
3. `rapidcsv::Document::GetCell`
    `GetCell` retrieves one CSV cell by row/column index or label, converting it to `T` via standard conversion (or a custom `ConvFunc`). Use zero-based indices; label overloads need matching headers. Examples show reading string/numeric values. No special caveats noted beyond `char` using the cell’s first byte. Its signature is:
    ```cpp
    /**
     * @brief   Get cell by index.
     * @param   pColumnIdx            zero-based column index.
     * @param   pRowIdx               zero-based row index.
     * @returns cell data.
     */
template<typename T>
    T GetCell(const size_t pColumnIdx, const size_t pRowIdx) const;
/**
     * @brief   Get cell by index.
     * @param   pColumnIdx            zero-based column index.
     * @param   pRowIdx               zero-based row index.
     * @param   pToVal                conversion function.
     * @returns cell data.
     */
template<typename T>
    T GetCell(const size_t pColumnIdx, const size_t pRowIdx, ConvFunc<T> pToVal) const;
/**
     * @brief   Get cell by name.
     * @param   pColumnName           column label name.
     * @param   pRowName              row label name.
     * @returns cell data.
     */
template<typename T>
    T GetCell(const std::string& pColumnName, const std::string& pRowName) const;
/**
     * @brief   Get cell by name.
     * @param   pColumnName           column label name.
     * @param   pRowName              row label name.
     * @param   pToVal                conversion function.
     * @returns cell data.
     */
template<typename T>
    T GetCell(const std::string& pColumnName, const std::string& pRowName, ConvFunc<T> pToVal) const;
/**
     * @brief   Get cell by column name and row index.
     * @param   pColumnName           column label name.
     * @param   pRowIdx               zero-based row index.
     * @returns cell data.
     */
template<typename T>
    T GetCell(const std::string& pColumnName, const size_t pRowIdx) const;
/**
     * @brief   Get cell by column name and row index.
     * @param   pColumnName           column label name.
     * @param   pRowIdx               zero-based row index.
     * @param   pToVal                conversion function.
     * @returns cell data.
     */
template<typename T>
    T GetCell(const std::string& pColumnName, const size_t pRowIdx, ConvFunc<T> pToVal) const;
/**
     * @brief   Get cell by column index and row name.
