    ```
12. `rapidcsv::Document::SetColumn`
    `SetColumn` writes a whole column into the CSV by index or name. It auto-expands rows/columns if needed, converts values to strings, and stores them starting after the header row/label offset. Use it with a vector matching the desired column data; missing space is created, existing cells are overwritten. Its signature is:
